          "date": "2026-11-20 21:50:40.000000000",
          "tz": -480
        },
        "subject": "LU-21228 lfs: find --report trees and owners",
        "message": "LU-21228 lfs: find --report trees and owners\n\nAdd tables of the users, groups and projects that own the most\nobjects and file bytes, and of the largest whole trees.  A tree\ncounts every entry and file byte below a directory, for directories\ndown to --report-depth levels below the root or a walk's start path,\n3 by default.  --report-top sets how many rows each table lists, 20\nby default.  Programs set fp_report_depth, and the top argument of\nllapi_find_report() now limits every table.\n\nA target scan reads every object's project ID.  A walk reads one only\nfor --projid, -printf or -ls, so its project tables list only those.\n\nTest-Parameters: ignore\nSigned-off-by: Hiroshi Nishida <hnishida@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I619d3be2d20540a020ba92795474146317b7d78a\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
